.TH XORCIST 1 "November 2026" "XORcist 2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
xorcist \- networking, diagnostics, and binary-data command-line utilities
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xorcist
.I net|diag|data|xor|secure|legacy-decrypt
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
XORcist performs offline IP planning and file operations, system DNS and
read-only route/interface inspection, and explicitly bounded TCP probes.
It includes authenticated file encryption using AES-256-GCM and scrypt.
The separate repeating-key XOR teaching tool is \fBnot secure encryption\fR.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B net
CIDR parsing, IPv4/IPv6 supernetting, range covering, overlap, VLSM and splitting.
.TP
.B diag
DNS and reverse lookups, interface/route inventory, mask and ACL helpers,
explicitly scoped TCP connection probes.
.TP
.B data
Base64 and hexadecimal encoding/decoding, binary inspection and comparison.
.TP
.B xor
Byte-wise repeating-key XOR demonstration only. Not for protecting secrets.
.TP
.B secure
Authenticated file encryption/decryption. Use a strong passphrase and keep
originals and backups until decryption is verified. Does not overwrite output.
.TP
.B legacy-decrypt
Read-only compatibility with 2019 Java XORcist data files.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
xorcist net summarize 192.168.1.1/24 192.168.2.1/24
xorcist diag dns localhost --family v4
xorcist diag interfaces
xorcist xor text --text 'Hello!' --key-hex 010203
xorcist secure encrypt --in file.bin --out file.xorc3
xorcist secure decrypt --in file.xorc3 --out recovered.bin
.fi
.SH SECURITY
Encryption relies on OpenSSL. Successful authentication checks file integrity,
not the identity or safety of the plaintext. Temporary plaintext may persist
after an abnormal termination. Never paste passwords into command arguments.
See SECURITY.md and M3_FILE_FORMAT.md for details.
.SH FILES
/usr/share/doc/xorcist/README.md, SECURITY.md and THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.
.SH BUGS
